<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-expectations-for-academic-integrity" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Academic Integrity</title>
  
    <p>
      Students are expected to present work that is their own without assistance from others. Academic integrity is fundamental to the learning process and is expected in all coursework.
    </p>

  <subsection xml:id="sec-scholastic-dishonesty">
    <title>Scholastic Dishonesty</title>
    
    <p>
      Midland College does not tolerate scholastic dishonesty or academic misconduct in any form.  Please read the Midland College Student Rights &amp; Responsibilities section in the <url href="https://www.midland.edu/about/public-info/scholastic-dishonesty.php">Midland College Catalog</url> for more information.
    </p>
  </subsection>

  <subsection xml:id="sec-ai-use-policy">
    <title>Artificial Intelligence Use Policy</title>
    <p>
      In this mathematics course, we will develop skills and knowledge that are essential to discover and practice on your own. Because the use of AI tools inhibits the development of these skills and knowledge, students are not allowed to use any AI tools in this course unless specifically stated on the assignment.
    </p>

    <p>
      Students are expected to present work that is their own without assistance from others, including automated tools. If you are unclear if something is an AI tool, please check with your instructor.
    </p>

    <p>
      Students are strongly encouraged to keep handwritten notes and mathematical computations in the event there is a concern about AI use. Using AI tools for any unstated purposes in this course will violate Midland College's academic integrity policy.
    </p>
  </subsection>

  <subsection xml:id="sec-smart-technology-use">
    <title>Smart Technology Use Policy</title>
    <p>
      Unless explicitly stated by your instructor, students should not use any smart technology for completing assignments in this course.  This includes but is not limited to cell phones, tablets, watches, and glasses.
    </p>
  </subsection>

</section>
